## Feature: Full-screen Bubbletea TUI for klarity init and klarity config

Replace the current huh-based init wizard in cmd/init.go with a full-screen
Bubbletea TUI. bubbletea is already a dependency. Do NOT change any scan
behavior or output — only the init wizard and config interactive menu.

---

## Architecture

Use the standard Bubbletea pattern:
  type model struct { ... }
  func (m model) Init() tea.Cmd
  func (m model) Update(msg tea.Msg) (tea.Model, tea.Cmd)
  func (m model) View() string

Run with: tea.NewProgram(initialModel(), tea.WithAltScreen())

tea.WithAltScreen() is the key — it takes over the full terminal, then
restores it when the program exits. This is the "BIOS-style" full screen.

---

## Phase structure

Five sequential phases. Phase pills shown at top of every screen.
Users cannot skip phases — flow is strictly linear forward/back.

  Phase 1: groupings    → show auto-detected env groupings table
  Phase 2: unmatched    → assign unmatched clusters one by one
  Phase 3: tiers        → confirm/change tier per environment
  Phase 4: default env  → select default_env (cursor-navigable list)
  Phase 5: save         → summary + save confirmation

Model fields:
  phase        int          // 0-4
  detected     config.DetectedEnvs
  selected     map[string][]string  // env → clusters (after user confirms)
  unmatched    []string     // clusters to assign
  unmatchedIdx int          // which unmatched cluster we're on
  unmatchedAssign map[string]string // cluster → env assignment
  tiers        map[string]string    // env → "critical" or "standard"
  tierCursor   int
  defaultEnv   string
  defCursor    int
  cursor       int          // generic cursor for list navigation
  inputVal     string       // text input for rename
  inputActive  bool         // whether text input has focus
  firstRun     bool         // show tip banner
  tipDismissed bool
  cfg          *config.Config
  err          error
  done         bool

---

## Key bindings (enforced in Update)

Global:
  ctrl+c, q (when not inputActive) → quit without saving
  esc → go back one phase (phase 0 = quit)

Phase 1 (groupings):
  ↑↓ → move cursor through env list (visual only, no action)
  enter, y → accept groupings, advance to phase 2
  e → enter edit mode (future — for now show "edit not yet available")

Phase 2 (unmatched):
  ↑↓ → move cursor through option list (existing groups + "new group" + "skip")
  enter → confirm assignment for current cluster, move to next
  type → when cursor on "new group", populate input
  backspace → edit input

Phase 3 (tiers):
  ↑↓ → move cursor through env list
  space → toggle tier for env under cursor (critical ↔ standard)
  enter → confirm all tiers, advance to phase 4

Phase 4 (default env):
  ↑↓ → move cursor through env list + "No default" option
  enter → select, advance to phase 5

Phase 5 (save):
  enter, s → save config and exit (if --scan flag, launch scan after)
  n → save only, no scan
  b, ← → go back to phase 4

