Every screen has the same structure:

  [logo]                    [phase pills: ● ○ ○ ○ ○]

  [phase title]

  [main content area — table or list or input]

  [help bar at bottom]

### Logo + phase pills (top, every screen)
  "klarity" in blue, right-aligned phase pills:
  done phases: filled green ●
  active phase: filled blue ● with label
  future phases: empty ○ dim

### Help bar (bottom, every screen — changes per phase)
Use lipgloss to render a dim horizontal rule then the key hints:
  Phase 1: "↑↓ move  ·  enter accept  ·  e edit  ·  esc cancel"
  Phase 2: "↑↓ move  ·  enter select  ·  type to rename  ·  esc back"
  Phase 3: "↑↓ move  ·  space toggle  ·  enter confirm  ·  esc back"
  Phase 4: "↑↓ move  ·  enter select  ·  esc back"
  Phase 5: "enter save & scan  ·  n save only  ·  esc back  ·  q quit"

### First-run tip banner (phase 1 only, dismissed on any keypress)
If firstRun && !tipDismissed, show above the main content:
  ┌─ tip ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ klarity init is keyboard-driven. ↑↓ move, enter confirm,  │
  │ esc goes back. Controls are shown at the bottom.           │
  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
Dismiss on any keypress. Track in config: settings.init_tip_shown: true
Never shown again after first run.

### Phase 1 — Groupings table
Columns: Environment | Tier | Clusters | Pattern
Critical rows: environment name in red lipgloss color
Cursor row: highlighted with subtle background
Show unmatched count below table: "N cluster(s) unmatched — assign next"
If 0 unmatched: skip phase 2 automatically

### Phase 2 — Unmatched assignment
Show current cluster name prominently
Options list:
  - all existing env names from detected + assigned so far
  - "new group →" with input field when selected
  - "skip (exclude from config)"
Cursor highlights selected option.
When "new group" selected and user types, update inputVal live.
Progress indicator: "Cluster 1 of N"

### Phase 3 — Tier confirmation
Table: Environment | Current Tier | Toggle
Cursor row highlighted. Space toggles tier.
Changed rows show tier in new color immediately.
Show legend: "● critical = shown first, red header  ○ standard = default"

### Phase 4 — Default environment
List of all environments + "No default — scan everything" at bottom.
Cursor-navigable. Selected item highlighted.
Show hint: "klarity will scan this by default. Use --env for others."

### Phase 5 — Save summary
Summary box:
  environments: N
  clusters: N
  default env: name (or "none")
  namespaces: all (excluding kube-system, kube-public, kube-node-lease, default)
  config path: ~/.klarityconfig.yaml

Save prompt with options highlighted.

