## Config interactive menu (klarity config)

Add a new interactive subcommand: klarity config (no subcommand = interactive menu)
Also full-screen Bubbletea, single screen (no phases):

  [logo]

  Config: ~/.klarityconfig.yaml
  Environments: N  ·  Clusters: N  ·  Default: name

  ┌─────────────────────────────────┐
  │  › Show config                  │
  │    Edit in $EDITOR              │
  │    Validate cluster connections │
  │    Change default environment   │
  │    Re-run init wizard           │
  │    Exit                         │
  └─────────────────────────────────┘

  ↑↓ move  ·  enter select  ·  q quit

Each option:
  "Show config" → prints config summary (exits full-screen, prints to stdout)
  "Edit in $EDITOR" → suspends bubbletea, opens editor, resumes
  "Validate cluster connections" → exits full-screen, runs existing validate logic
  "Change default environment" → shows env list inline, updates config
  "Re-run init wizard" → exits full-screen, runs init
  "Exit" → quit

This replaces the current klarity config behavior where no subcommand
currently falls through to help text. klarity config show, edit, validate,
path still work as before — the interactive menu is only when no subcommand given.

